{%- doc -%}
  Classifies one entry of the custom.customer_photos file-reference list so the
  PDP Redo customer photos section can count and render it.

  Echoes one of:
    image      - an image file (has width/height, render with image_tag)
    video      - a video picked from Content > Files (has sources, video_tag)
    file_video - a generic file whose URL is a video (render a plain <video>)
    ""         - anything else (a PDF, say) - the caller skips it

  A file_reference list hands back a different Liquid object per file type, so
  the type is inferred from what the object actually responds to rather than
  from a media_type field that only some of them carry.

  @param {object} media - one entry of the metafield list

  @example
    {%- capture kind -%}{%- render 'pdp-redo-customer-media-kind', media: media -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign kind = kind | strip -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign kind = ''

  if media.width
    assign kind = 'image'
  elsif media.sources.size > 0
    assign kind = 'video'
  else
    assign media_url = media.url | default: '' | downcase | split: '?' | first
    if media_url contains '.mp4' or media_url contains '.mov' or media_url contains '.webm' or media_url contains '.m4v'
      assign kind = 'file_video'
    endif
  endif
-%}{{ kind }}
